1
00:00:00,567 --> 00:00:03,002
(Scenes with child actors were filmed
safely with guardians and staff present.)

2
00:00:48,048 --> 00:00:49,649
Calvin offered me...

3
00:00:50,452 --> 00:00:52,819
the head of a new business venture.

4
00:01:27,421 --> 00:01:28,388
What is it?

5
00:01:28,522 --> 00:01:29,955
Just checking if you were asleep.

6
00:01:29,956 --> 00:01:31,390
Go back to sleep. I'll get going.

7
00:01:32,025 --> 00:01:33,092
Wait.

8
00:01:35,196 --> 00:01:36,963
Am I too late?

9
00:01:37,430 --> 00:01:38,765
Too late for what?

10
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:41,267
To go to Mi Young.

11
00:01:43,237 --> 00:01:46,905
I know how ridiculous I look
acting like this now.

12
00:01:46,906 --> 00:01:48,474
- But still...
- You are late.

13
00:01:49,276 --> 00:01:51,011
You're far too late.

14
00:01:51,012 --> 00:01:52,512
So get moving while you still can.

15
00:01:53,680 --> 00:01:54,613
Hurry up.

16
00:01:59,753 --> 00:02:00,987
Go.

17
00:02:00,988 --> 00:02:03,055
And don't come back here.

18
00:02:03,524 --> 00:02:05,758
- Seung Ho.
- Hurry.

19
00:02:35,522 --> 00:02:36,555
Wait.

20
00:02:37,457 --> 00:02:38,490
Come on.

21
00:02:41,828 --> 00:02:42,961
Here.

22
00:03:06,920 --> 00:03:07,853
Even after...

23
00:03:09,123 --> 00:03:10,957
my husband buried Dal Rae there,

24
00:03:12,059 --> 00:03:14,260
he never went back during the season...

25
00:03:15,629 --> 00:03:17,029
when the azaleas bloomed.

26
00:03:19,700 --> 00:03:21,400
I know deep down...

27
00:03:22,035 --> 00:03:26,005
that he just couldn't
bring himself to face...

28
00:03:27,874 --> 00:03:29,575
those beautiful flowers.

29
00:03:32,079 --> 00:03:33,112
Because...

30
00:03:35,849 --> 00:03:37,950
we're still tied to each other.

31
00:03:40,087 --> 00:03:42,889
Dal Rae is the bond
that holds us together.

32
00:03:46,126 --> 00:03:48,794
We were husband and wife,

33
00:03:49,597 --> 00:03:51,197
and we were parents.

34
00:04:08,448 --> 00:04:10,816
What brings you here so late?

35
00:04:14,355 --> 00:04:15,521
Won Ho.

36
00:04:16,523 --> 00:04:18,290
Let's go together sometime.

37
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:21,660
When the azaleas bloom,

38
00:04:24,064 --> 00:04:25,998
let's go see them together.

39
00:04:41,648 --> 00:04:42,648
Let's go.

40
00:04:46,086 --> 00:04:47,219
Let's go together.

41
00:04:49,923 --> 00:04:51,223
We'll go together...

42
00:04:54,194 --> 00:04:56,896
to visit Dal Rae.

43
00:05:35,301 --> 00:05:36,269
In that moment,

44
00:05:37,170 --> 00:05:38,704
everything that had happened...

45
00:05:39,106 --> 00:05:40,539
felt like a dream.

46
00:05:46,880 --> 00:05:48,682
As if waking from a long nightmare...

47
00:05:49,850 --> 00:05:52,852
to finally find each other again.

48
00:06:01,962 --> 00:06:03,629
As if we had never once...

49
00:06:04,064 --> 00:06:06,399
hated each other.

50
00:06:12,773 --> 00:06:14,940
We wanted each other more desperately...

51
00:06:15,809 --> 00:06:17,009
than ever before.

52
00:06:24,150 --> 00:06:25,150
As if we'd never...

53
00:06:26,286 --> 00:06:27,620
push each other away again.

54
00:06:58,218 --> 00:07:00,053
It must have been unbearable...

55
00:07:02,123 --> 00:07:03,890
having to say goodbye
to Dal Rae like that.

56
00:07:04,791 --> 00:07:06,325
Why ask me that now?

57
00:07:07,794 --> 00:07:09,695
I can't even begin to imagine...

58
00:07:11,464 --> 00:07:13,131
what you went through.

59
00:07:14,334 --> 00:07:17,169
I told myself we'd meet again someday.

60
00:07:21,441 --> 00:07:23,776
You, me, and Dal Rae.

61
00:07:26,246 --> 00:07:27,713
I believed that someday,

62
00:07:29,049 --> 00:07:30,817
the three of us would be together again.

63
00:07:32,520 --> 00:07:34,321
That was the only way I could keep going.

64
00:07:35,655 --> 00:07:37,589
So, Mi Young,

65
00:07:38,491 --> 00:07:40,192
please let go of the pain now.

66
00:07:44,531 --> 00:07:45,626
Because someday,

67
00:07:46,867 --> 00:07:48,401
we'll all be together again.

68
00:08:10,423 --> 00:08:11,623
What on earth is all this?

69
00:08:18,598 --> 00:08:19,598
Wait.

70
00:08:21,067 --> 00:08:22,367
Has Mr. Kang...

71
00:08:23,236 --> 00:08:26,171
harbored feelings for Mi Young
this whole time?

72
00:08:28,808 --> 00:08:30,575
What am I supposed to do with this?

73
00:08:31,144 --> 00:08:33,946
Should I tell Mi Young? Or Mr. Ji?

74
00:08:35,115 --> 00:08:36,415
No.

75
00:08:36,416 --> 00:08:38,651
Finding this out would
tear them both apart.

76
00:08:41,688 --> 00:08:44,356
Right. Just in case.

77
00:09:21,695 --> 00:09:22,595
Did you sleep well?

78
00:09:22,929 --> 00:09:23,762
Yes.

79
00:09:24,164 --> 00:09:25,732
What's all this out of nowhere?

80
00:09:31,371 --> 00:09:32,237
Here.

81
00:09:36,409 --> 00:09:37,642
My husband is...

82
00:09:37,745 --> 00:09:40,246
even more handsome on the inside
than he is on the outside.

83
00:09:40,948 --> 00:09:45,651
He even made me fresh juice
before leaving for work today.

84
00:09:59,466 --> 00:10:01,534
- What is this?
- Why? Don't you like it?

85
00:10:02,035 --> 00:10:02,868
I mean,

86
00:10:03,870 --> 00:10:05,514
what did you put in this? It's so good!

87
00:10:05,672 --> 00:10:07,607
You startled me for a second.

88
00:10:08,008 --> 00:10:10,810
I was extra picky
when choosing the oranges.

89
00:10:11,177 --> 00:10:12,444
Good, right?

90
00:10:21,087 --> 00:10:24,224
Are you going to look at me like that
at the office too?

91
00:10:24,657 --> 00:10:26,758
Was I making it that obvious?

92
00:10:29,496 --> 00:10:30,429
But...

93
00:10:30,964 --> 00:10:32,364
what do we do now?

94
00:10:32,667 --> 00:10:33,566
What?

95
00:10:38,571 --> 00:10:40,705
Look at the time!

96
00:10:40,706 --> 00:10:42,575
We need to hurry and get ready for work.

97
00:10:42,576 --> 00:10:43,442
Right.

98
00:11:26,219 --> 00:11:27,653
Hold on.

99
00:11:27,921 --> 00:11:29,287
I'm sorry.

100
00:11:29,956 --> 00:11:32,558
- Hurry up.
- Thank you.

101
00:11:33,626 --> 00:11:34,726
I'm sorry!

102
00:11:43,570 --> 00:11:45,104
All right.

103
00:11:49,209 --> 00:11:50,075
See you then.

104
00:12:00,019 --> 00:12:01,052
Ms. Song?

105
00:12:02,054 --> 00:12:04,489
Yes, Mr. Kang? What's up?

106
00:12:05,158 --> 00:12:07,459
Why are you doubling up on work?

107
00:12:11,331 --> 00:12:12,231
What?

108
00:12:12,499 --> 00:12:15,100
I already set all of that up.

109
00:12:17,104 --> 00:12:19,838
Oh, you already took care of it?

110
00:12:20,506 --> 00:12:21,841
Are you feeling under the weather?

111
00:12:23,009 --> 00:12:23,875
No.

112
00:12:24,911 --> 00:12:25,811
Well...

113
00:12:27,213 --> 00:12:28,079
Mr. Kang,

114
00:12:28,781 --> 00:12:30,081
how come...

115
00:12:30,616 --> 00:12:32,551
you never date anyone?

116
00:12:33,119 --> 00:12:33,985
What?

117
00:12:34,254 --> 00:12:37,957
I've just never seen you with someone.

118
00:12:38,191 --> 00:12:41,094
I can't date just anyone
just because I'm lonely.

119
00:12:41,961 --> 00:12:44,197
My standards are pretty high, you know.

120
00:12:44,632 --> 00:12:47,666
So your standards are through the roof.

121
00:12:48,835 --> 00:12:51,236
Now it all makes sense.

122
00:12:52,005 --> 00:12:52,905
What?

123
00:12:52,906 --> 00:12:54,406
I'm just saying, clearly,

124
00:12:54,775 --> 00:12:57,709
you have very high standards.
Impossibly high.

125
00:13:01,682 --> 00:13:04,550
Ms. Baek is running a little late today,
isn't she?

126
00:13:04,884 --> 00:13:07,420
Can't even wait a few minutes
without missing her that much?

127
00:13:08,521 --> 00:13:10,665
- Hello.
- Good morning.

128
00:13:10,690 --> 00:13:12,057
Speak of the devil.

129
00:13:12,759 --> 00:13:14,760
Ms. Baek, good morning.

130
00:13:14,928 --> 00:13:15,860
Good morning.

131
00:13:15,861 --> 00:13:18,506
Did you finish sorting those first-half
sales figures I asked for yesterday?

132
00:13:18,531 --> 00:13:22,234
How on earth did I not see it sooner?

133
00:13:23,136 --> 00:13:24,069
Yes, all done.

134
00:13:24,471 --> 00:13:27,439
I want construction finished
as fast as possible...

135
00:13:27,508 --> 00:13:29,697
so Calvin Wedding can host
its opening ceremony...

136
00:13:29,721 --> 00:13:31,510
before the month ends.

137
00:13:32,378 --> 00:13:35,113
I know it's a tight deadline,
which is why I'm turning to you.

138
00:13:35,381 --> 00:13:37,615
Bring in subcontractors
or add more shifts if you have to.

139
00:13:37,750 --> 00:13:39,117
Do whatever it takes.

140
00:13:39,685 --> 00:13:41,453
I will cover all the costs.

141
00:13:55,935 --> 00:13:57,370
Let me make you an official offer.

142
00:13:57,870 --> 00:14:00,306
I want you to head up Calvin Wedding...

143
00:14:01,040 --> 00:14:02,475
as the director of this new venture.

144
00:14:05,078 --> 00:14:06,745
Thank you.

145
00:14:08,449 --> 00:14:11,316
But I have to turn it down.

146
00:14:11,984 --> 00:14:13,518
Even if it's strictly business,

147
00:14:14,155 --> 00:14:16,788
I'm not sure moving forward with you
like this is the right thing to do.

148
00:14:17,423 --> 00:14:19,267
And I don't know
if I'll ever be able to...

149
00:14:19,292 --> 00:14:21,426
truly walk away from J＆WHITE.

150
00:14:28,801 --> 00:14:31,068
Well, that settles it. It's over!

151
00:14:31,069 --> 00:14:32,371
What do you mean, it's over?

152
00:14:32,372 --> 00:14:34,873
Am I wrong? You two cleared the air,

153
00:14:34,874 --> 00:14:37,041
and you even spent the night together!

154
00:14:37,711 --> 00:14:39,311
Someone might hear you. Keep it down.

155
00:14:39,445 --> 00:14:40,779
So what?

156
00:14:40,913 --> 00:14:43,747
What's wrong with a married couple
spending the night together?

157
00:14:43,748 --> 00:14:46,317
That's not what I meant.

158
00:14:46,786 --> 00:14:48,420
Look at that glow.

159
00:14:49,154 --> 00:14:51,790
Someone clearly had an amazing night.

160
00:14:52,458 --> 00:14:54,993
Just look at the bright colors
you're wearing today!

161
00:14:55,194 --> 00:14:56,361
Come on, spill.

162
00:14:56,496 --> 00:14:57,963
Tell me everything.

163
00:14:57,964 --> 00:14:59,565
Stop it.

164
00:15:01,735 --> 00:15:05,704
The two of you were never going
to break apart that easily.

165
00:15:06,406 --> 00:15:08,841
I'm so glad I kept my mouth shut.

166
00:15:09,609 --> 00:15:10,843
Kept your mouth shut about what?

167
00:15:11,144 --> 00:15:13,612
Oh, nothing.

168
00:15:14,280 --> 00:15:18,083
Anyway, call your divorce lawyer
right now.

169
00:15:18,084 --> 00:15:19,685
Tell her you're calling it off.

170
00:15:20,420 --> 00:15:22,187
You're not seriously...

171
00:15:22,188 --> 00:15:24,622
still going through with it
after last night, are you?

172
00:15:25,091 --> 00:15:26,158
The thing is,

173
00:15:26,627 --> 00:15:29,862
I still don't know
where Won Ho's head is at.

174
00:15:30,196 --> 00:15:31,129
What?

175
00:15:31,363 --> 00:15:34,532
Won Ho waited three years for me.

176
00:15:34,968 --> 00:15:37,235
This time, it's my turn to wait.

177
00:15:37,769 --> 00:15:40,173
I'll wait until he's completely
certain about how he feels.

178
00:15:40,740 --> 00:15:44,309
So you're really not going
to divorce Mi Young?

179
00:15:44,544 --> 00:15:45,510
No.

180
00:15:50,650 --> 00:15:52,451
What's with that look?

181
00:15:53,186 --> 00:15:54,119
Nothing.

182
00:15:54,921 --> 00:15:57,121
That's wonderful. Congratulations.

183
00:15:57,122 --> 00:15:59,557
It's a little early for congratulations.

184
00:15:59,558 --> 00:16:02,460
I need to sit down and talk things through
with Mi Young first.

185
00:16:03,262 --> 00:16:06,064
If we're on the same page,
I'll contact the lawyer...

186
00:16:06,332 --> 00:16:07,399
and drop the case.

187
00:16:07,934 --> 00:16:08,867
Still,

188
00:16:09,435 --> 00:16:11,703
don't you think rushing
into that might be...

189
00:16:12,672 --> 00:16:13,872
a bit risky?

190
00:16:15,575 --> 00:16:16,842
Risky? How?

191
00:16:17,143 --> 00:16:19,044
Think about it.

192
00:16:19,979 --> 00:16:21,846
Mi Young filed for divorce
in the first place.

193
00:16:22,449 --> 00:16:24,416
And looking at what she wrote
in that filing,

194
00:16:24,751 --> 00:16:26,219
do you honestly think her feelings...

195
00:16:26,953 --> 00:16:28,854
could just flip overnight like that?

196
00:16:31,023 --> 00:16:31,924
You might have a point.

197
00:16:32,191 --> 00:16:34,160
Plus, the situation with Calvin
is still up in the air.

198
00:16:34,426 --> 00:16:36,162
Instead of laying it all out right away,

199
00:16:36,529 --> 00:16:38,264
why not sort things out
one step at a time...

200
00:16:38,832 --> 00:16:40,164
and pick the right moment?

201
00:16:48,140 --> 00:16:50,642
What are you waiting on so impatiently?

202
00:16:50,810 --> 00:16:52,577
Never mind.

203
00:17:01,621 --> 00:17:03,055
(Jihwaja Motel)

204
00:17:03,056 --> 00:17:04,957
Excuse me. Counselor!

205
00:17:05,591 --> 00:17:06,724
Counselor!

206
00:17:09,829 --> 00:17:10,762
Counselor.

207
00:17:12,031 --> 00:17:14,332
Oh, hello.

208
00:17:14,767 --> 00:17:16,367
Why are you running away from me?

209
00:17:17,336 --> 00:17:19,337
Me? Who said I'm running away?

210
00:17:19,472 --> 00:17:22,006
You would've walked away
if I hadn't called out.

211
00:17:23,744 --> 00:17:25,144
I've been waiting for you.

212
00:17:26,612 --> 00:17:28,414
I wanted to apologize
for what happened the other day.

213
00:17:30,049 --> 00:17:31,015
It's fine.

214
00:17:31,484 --> 00:17:32,718
You don't need to apologize.

215
00:17:35,221 --> 00:17:36,387
You must be freezing.

216
00:17:45,031 --> 00:17:45,964
Here.

217
00:17:47,534 --> 00:17:50,168
These are the recordings
from while you were away.

218
00:17:50,436 --> 00:17:52,371
What you've been looking for
should be in there.

219
00:17:53,539 --> 00:17:54,507
Thank you.

220
00:17:56,709 --> 00:17:57,642
- Counselor...
- Well...

221
00:17:59,479 --> 00:18:00,746
Go ahead.

222
00:18:00,847 --> 00:18:01,780
Okay.

223
00:18:02,081 --> 00:18:04,282
- Counselor...
- Hey!

224
00:18:04,685 --> 00:18:06,399
You have some nerve to show up here!

225
00:18:06,423 --> 00:18:07,152
Mom.

226
00:18:07,321 --> 00:18:09,187
You're Mi Young's lawyer, aren't you?

227
00:18:09,788 --> 00:18:12,124
- I wasn't expecting to see you here.
- Let's just go inside.

228
00:18:12,291 --> 00:18:13,524
What are you doing here?

229
00:18:13,525 --> 00:18:15,460
What are you snooping around
for this time?

230
00:18:15,461 --> 00:18:17,028
I think there's been a misunderstanding.

231
00:18:17,029 --> 00:18:18,463
What misunderstanding?

232
00:18:19,065 --> 00:18:21,466
Did I misunderstand that ridiculous
divorce complaint you served us with too?

233
00:18:21,868 --> 00:18:24,535
Painting my precious son
as some shameless lowlife!

234
00:18:24,536 --> 00:18:27,605
Get lost, and don't you dare come back!

235
00:18:30,476 --> 00:18:31,409
Good grief.

236
00:18:32,578 --> 00:18:35,013
Counselor. Wait!

237
00:18:35,380 --> 00:18:37,717
How can she show her face here
without a shred of shame?

238
00:18:38,384 --> 00:18:40,419
- This is all your fault, Mom!
- What?

239
00:18:40,720 --> 00:18:42,688
Just like you ran that woman off,

240
00:18:43,089 --> 00:18:44,756
you drove Mi Young away too.

241
00:18:45,091 --> 00:18:48,360
Because of you, Won Ho and I
are going to die alone!

242
00:18:48,361 --> 00:18:50,896
What's gotten into you all of a sudden?
Did you eat something bad?

243
00:18:51,030 --> 00:18:52,297
I'm not coming home tonight.

244
00:18:52,865 --> 00:18:54,065
Don't bother looking for me.

245
00:18:55,735 --> 00:18:57,703
- Counselor!
- Where do you think you're going?

246
00:18:58,337 --> 00:18:59,437
Unbelievable!

247
00:19:01,440 --> 00:19:02,407
That little brat.

248
00:19:08,214 --> 00:19:10,248
It's really coming down out here.

249
00:19:11,817 --> 00:19:14,652
- This place must be really popular.
- Totally.

250
00:19:20,660 --> 00:19:22,127
Look how adorable you are.

251
00:19:23,029 --> 00:19:24,029
Stop that.

252
00:19:24,297 --> 00:19:26,098
Hello!

253
00:19:28,134 --> 00:19:30,569
Wait, did you catch that?
She just smiled at me.

254
00:19:32,939 --> 00:19:34,439
She really is precious.

255
00:19:35,074 --> 00:19:37,676
Such a little angel.

256
00:19:42,214 --> 00:19:44,482
We'll take two bowls of pho, please.

257
00:19:44,885 --> 00:19:46,451
Mi Young doesn't like cilantro.

258
00:19:46,452 --> 00:19:48,420
Please make one regular bowl, no cilantro,

259
00:19:48,421 --> 00:19:50,055
and one large bowl with extra cilantro.

260
00:19:50,823 --> 00:19:52,590
Won Ho, you like spring rolls, right?

261
00:19:52,692 --> 00:19:54,326
- Let's get an order of spring rolls too.
- Of course.

262
00:19:54,694 --> 00:19:56,561
Anything else I can get you?

263
00:19:56,763 --> 00:19:58,197
- Extra mung bean sprouts, please.
- Extra mung bean sprouts, please.

264
00:20:10,876 --> 00:20:14,712
When was the last time
just the two of us had a meal?

265
00:20:15,214 --> 00:20:17,382
A meal or pho?

266
00:20:18,217 --> 00:20:19,217
Come to think of it,

267
00:20:19,886 --> 00:20:22,553
it's been forever
since we had a meal together.

268
00:20:22,755 --> 00:20:23,688
I know.

269
00:20:25,324 --> 00:20:27,057
Same for traveling together.

270
00:20:27,494 --> 00:20:29,561
Was our honeymoon the last time?

271
00:20:31,297 --> 00:20:32,397
We've been busy.

272
00:20:32,632 --> 00:20:34,265
Still, even if we were busy...

273
00:20:35,168 --> 00:20:37,535
No wonder you divorced me.

274
00:20:42,575 --> 00:20:43,475
Well.

275
00:20:44,477 --> 00:20:46,711
Speaking of divorce...

276
00:20:56,422 --> 00:20:57,989
Instead of confessing everything at once,

277
00:20:58,257 --> 00:20:59,857
why don't you wait for the right time,

278
00:21:00,660 --> 00:21:01,926
and handle things one by one?

279
00:21:03,829 --> 00:21:06,097
I regret so many things.

280
00:21:08,634 --> 00:21:09,534
I see.

281
00:21:11,303 --> 00:21:12,303
So, here's the thing.

282
00:21:14,073 --> 00:21:16,174
Please wait a little longer, Mi Young.

283
00:21:18,110 --> 00:21:20,545
Can you wait just a little longer...

284
00:21:20,946 --> 00:21:23,849
until I'm ready to tell you?

285
00:21:26,018 --> 00:21:26,818
Okay.

286
00:21:27,621 --> 00:21:28,553
I will.

287
00:21:30,023 --> 00:21:31,389
Let's eat before it gets cold.

288
00:21:41,293 --> 00:21:45,203
I want to tell you about something
we've prepared for you.

289
00:21:45,204 --> 00:21:46,337
Hello.

290
00:21:46,772 --> 00:21:50,042
During this event,
customers who visit our shop...

291
00:21:50,043 --> 00:21:51,886
will receive this keychain as a gift.

292
00:21:51,887 --> 00:21:52,977
Isn't it cute?

293
00:21:53,614 --> 00:21:54,713
If you have this...

294
00:21:54,714 --> 00:21:56,782
You just have to visit to get one.

295
00:21:57,149 --> 00:21:58,382
Ta-da!

296
00:21:58,685 --> 00:22:00,085
What's the best part about working late?

297
00:22:00,686 --> 00:22:02,720
Late-night snacks!

298
00:22:07,059 --> 00:22:09,160
Eating late-night snacks
while working overtime.

299
00:22:11,630 --> 00:22:13,898
- Who eats chicken with that?
- I like this combination.

300
00:22:14,433 --> 00:22:15,666
Try it. It's good.

301
00:22:16,502 --> 00:22:18,236
What did we decide on for the concept?

302
00:22:18,237 --> 00:22:19,871
Look at the next page.

303
00:22:21,373 --> 00:22:22,940
I like it.

304
00:22:22,941 --> 00:22:25,276
Something that fits the season.

305
00:22:25,277 --> 00:22:26,811
Could you look into it for us?

306
00:22:26,812 --> 00:22:28,212
First of all...

307
00:22:30,153 --> 00:22:32,150
Something that really fits the season.

308
00:22:32,151 --> 00:22:34,618
What flowers would go well with it?

309
00:22:36,088 --> 00:22:37,790
Pink would be nice.

310
00:22:41,827 --> 00:22:43,762
- What should we eat?
- Soup?

311
00:22:43,763 --> 00:22:45,096
Sounds good.

312
00:22:45,264 --> 00:22:46,798
Can I send you the materials by tomorrow?

313
00:22:46,799 --> 00:22:49,434
Yes. You go ahead.
I'm going to the bathroom.

314
00:22:51,337 --> 00:22:53,271
- Okay.
- Let's do this.

315
00:22:53,272 --> 00:22:55,774
I left my phone behind.

316
00:22:56,008 --> 00:22:57,008
I'll go ahead.

317
00:23:12,925 --> 00:23:14,492
I don't know. I'm good with anything.

318
00:23:15,227 --> 00:23:16,494
- Something warm?
- Great.

319
00:23:43,222 --> 00:23:46,291
I got you!

320
00:23:55,000 --> 00:23:57,601
Princess, wake up.

321
00:23:57,602 --> 00:23:59,570
The sun is already high in the sky.

322
00:23:59,739 --> 00:24:02,440
Get up and get ready for work.

323
00:24:02,942 --> 00:24:04,042
What time is it?

324
00:24:04,243 --> 00:24:06,010
You have enough time to get up
and get ready.

325
00:24:16,288 --> 00:24:17,322
(Attorney Jeon Chi Hyun)

326
00:24:17,323 --> 00:24:18,890
You must be busy these days.

327
00:24:19,191 --> 00:24:20,892
Are you free today?

328
00:24:23,930 --> 00:24:24,762
(Attorney Bae Su Ji)

329
00:24:24,763 --> 00:24:26,163
Are you dead or something?

330
00:24:31,271 --> 00:24:32,170
- Hey.
- Hey.

331
00:24:33,772 --> 00:24:34,638
You go first.

332
00:24:35,240 --> 00:24:36,608
No, you go first.

333
00:24:39,979 --> 00:24:40,812
Well.

334
00:24:42,581 --> 00:24:44,415
About our trial...

335
00:24:45,084 --> 00:24:47,519
What about it?

336
00:24:48,687 --> 00:24:51,188
I've been thinking about it a lot.

337
00:24:53,993 --> 00:24:55,927
We should postpone it, right?

338
00:24:56,128 --> 00:24:57,361
Postpone it?

339
00:24:57,830 --> 00:25:00,631
Yes, what do you think we should do?

340
00:25:00,966 --> 00:25:03,901
He's the textbook avoidant type.

341
00:25:05,437 --> 00:25:07,671
He kept putting off the divorce too.

342
00:25:08,173 --> 00:25:12,210
What on earth is he thinking?

343
00:25:13,413 --> 00:25:17,281
Does he want to make
things work with me again?

344
00:25:17,983 --> 00:25:18,883
Or...

345
00:25:19,718 --> 00:25:21,886
is he still trying to decide?

346
00:25:24,590 --> 00:25:25,924
You led the way...

347
00:25:26,626 --> 00:25:29,127
and brought
the divorce proceedings this far.

348
00:25:30,062 --> 00:25:31,863
Do you think things will be
any different now?

349
00:25:32,831 --> 00:25:33,715
Remember...

350
00:25:34,201 --> 00:25:35,933
where you are right now.

351
00:25:37,404 --> 00:25:41,172
You're just about to come out
of a dark tunnel.

352
00:25:42,074 --> 00:25:44,842
You're almost there.

353
00:25:49,648 --> 00:25:51,883
Mr. Ji, where are you right now?

354
00:25:52,283 --> 00:25:53,817
You weren't at the studio.

355
00:25:54,588 --> 00:25:56,688
Are you not coming to the motel anymore?

356
00:25:57,590 --> 00:25:59,157
Let's talk over dinner.

357
00:25:59,558 --> 00:26:01,326
I have so much to tell you.

358
00:26:01,627 --> 00:26:04,162
Read your messages, will you?

359
00:26:18,644 --> 00:26:19,978
Ignoring me again?

360
00:27:23,475 --> 00:27:24,508
No way.

361
00:27:44,663 --> 00:27:47,632
Have you stooped to going
through someone else's things now?

362
00:27:47,800 --> 00:27:48,700
It was you, right?

363
00:27:49,802 --> 00:27:52,937
You were the one who pushed me
off the cliff, weren't you?

364
00:27:53,739 --> 00:27:54,672
That again?

365
00:27:55,774 --> 00:27:56,674
This.

366
00:27:57,410 --> 00:28:00,845
You had this the day
you pushed me off the cliff, didn't you?

367
00:28:00,846 --> 00:28:01,913
- Give that to me.
- No.

368
00:28:02,514 --> 00:28:04,448
I'm taking this to the police.

369
00:28:04,583 --> 00:28:07,151
I'm going to put you behind bars.

370
00:28:30,809 --> 00:28:32,475
I should've finished you off back then.

371
00:28:33,513 --> 00:28:35,780
- What?
- I regret it now.

372
00:28:37,349 --> 00:28:38,315
That day,

373
00:28:39,518 --> 00:28:40,952
if I'd dealt with you properly,

374
00:28:42,421 --> 00:28:44,222
I wouldn't have to put up with all this.

375
00:28:44,890 --> 00:28:46,858
Why are you doing this to me?

376
00:28:47,059 --> 00:28:48,659
You started this.

377
00:28:50,262 --> 00:28:51,295
What's going on?

378
00:28:51,497 --> 00:28:52,664
If you don't stop,

379
00:28:53,665 --> 00:28:55,197
I'll have no choice but to go all the way.

380
00:28:56,068 --> 00:28:58,435
Are you really saying you'll kill me?

381
00:28:58,436 --> 00:28:59,637
You know better than anyone.

382
00:29:02,274 --> 00:29:03,340
That day,

383
00:29:04,443 --> 00:29:05,476
you got lucky.

384
00:29:29,935 --> 00:29:31,502
(An Hee Ju)

385
00:29:36,575 --> 00:29:37,742
Shouldn't you answer it?

386
00:29:39,144 --> 00:29:41,011
No. It's a call I don't need to take.

387
00:29:41,313 --> 00:29:42,480
That's not good.

388
00:29:42,481 --> 00:29:44,515
Just running away instead of facing it.

389
00:29:45,619 --> 00:29:47,251
Also, to your wife.

390
00:29:47,653 --> 00:29:50,822
Tell her you don't want a divorce
and you want to get back together.

391
00:29:50,823 --> 00:29:52,657
Be a man and deal with it.

392
00:29:53,592 --> 00:29:54,725
I know.

393
00:29:54,726 --> 00:29:57,028
Then what are you hesitating for?

394
00:29:57,496 --> 00:30:01,499
I can't let this be all about what I want.

395
00:30:02,701 --> 00:30:03,601
What do you mean?

396
00:30:04,069 --> 00:30:05,169
My wife is...

397
00:30:05,938 --> 00:30:07,739
more fragile than she looks.

398
00:30:08,674 --> 00:30:10,741
What if she's only going along
with everything...

399
00:30:10,742 --> 00:30:13,110
because she's afraid I'll get hurt?

400
00:30:15,514 --> 00:30:16,614
And she could...

401
00:30:18,217 --> 00:30:20,184
find someone better than me.

402
00:30:21,187 --> 00:30:23,554
Maybe I'm just holding her back.

403
00:30:24,156 --> 00:30:25,156
What about you?

404
00:30:25,591 --> 00:30:27,325
Are you sure you won't regret it?

405
00:30:28,393 --> 00:30:29,760
Honestly,

406
00:30:30,095 --> 00:30:32,497
I've never once...

407
00:30:33,999 --> 00:30:35,299
wanted to divorce my wife.

408
00:30:37,870 --> 00:30:40,004
Even when we fought
like we wanted to kill each other,

409
00:30:40,005 --> 00:30:42,173
even when we treated
each other like strangers,

410
00:30:43,876 --> 00:30:46,244
I really couldn't imagine
living as complete strangers.

411
00:30:47,579 --> 00:30:48,746
That's what I learned.

412
00:30:49,348 --> 00:30:50,281
My goodness.

413
00:30:51,684 --> 00:30:54,585
You used to act
like you didn't care at all.

414
00:30:56,188 --> 00:30:57,822
That was just me being pathetic.

415
00:30:58,657 --> 00:31:00,157
My stupid pride got in the way.

416
00:31:00,359 --> 00:31:03,061
But if you just sit around like this,
she's going to misunderstand.

417
00:31:04,096 --> 00:31:06,130
What will you do if this
actually goes all the way?

418
00:31:09,335 --> 00:31:11,202
That's what I'm struggling with.

419
00:31:12,037 --> 00:31:14,173
I want my wife to take my hand...

420
00:31:14,174 --> 00:31:16,007
because she genuinely wants to.

421
00:31:16,409 --> 00:31:17,608
I'm trying to figure out...

422
00:31:17,609 --> 00:31:20,644
how I can make her understand
how I really feel.

423
00:31:20,645 --> 00:31:23,247
Do you have any ideas?

424
00:31:27,686 --> 00:31:28,686
I'm sorry,

425
00:31:30,022 --> 00:31:33,024
but this is something
neither Mr. Kwon nor I can solve for you.

426
00:31:33,525 --> 00:31:34,492
Why not?

427
00:31:34,995 --> 00:31:36,594
Because both Mr. Kwon and I are...

428
00:31:38,196 --> 00:31:39,396
lifelong bachelors.

429
00:31:43,635 --> 00:31:47,137
For stuff like this,
actual experience is the real deal.

430
00:31:48,540 --> 00:31:49,896
Do you know anyone around you...

431
00:31:50,140 --> 00:31:51,795
who's an expert...

432
00:31:52,665 --> 00:31:53,878
in this field?

433
00:31:55,581 --> 00:31:57,315
Someone around me with experience.

434
00:31:59,451 --> 00:32:00,384
Actually, I do.

435
00:32:01,653 --> 00:32:02,820
Someone very close to me.

436
00:32:10,562 --> 00:32:14,665
Whoever they are,
they must be crazy to lose you.

437
00:32:15,534 --> 00:32:16,934
Someone this lovable...

438
00:32:21,707 --> 00:32:22,707
Duck down!

439
00:32:23,109 --> 00:32:24,141
Hurry!

440
00:32:30,115 --> 00:32:32,450
What do you think you're doing here?

441
00:32:32,784 --> 00:32:34,618
You're Mi Young's attorney, aren't you?

442
00:32:35,220 --> 00:32:36,353
Nice to see you here.

443
00:32:36,354 --> 00:32:38,021
Are you here to snoop around?

444
00:32:38,022 --> 00:32:40,891
Get the hell out of here
and don't ever come back.

445
00:32:55,808 --> 00:32:57,641
Get a grip, man.

446
00:32:58,444 --> 00:32:59,977
Would you come back
if you were in her shoes?

447
00:33:00,813 --> 00:33:02,914
Yes, I came back.

448
00:33:03,414 --> 00:33:05,615
What the heck?
I told you not to come back.

449
00:33:05,616 --> 00:33:07,518
- Well...
- Get out.

450
00:33:07,519 --> 00:33:10,454
- I've been thinking...
- You're banned from this place.

451
00:33:10,990 --> 00:33:12,790
- Wait.
- You're banned.

452
00:33:12,791 --> 00:33:15,192
Even if you have to die,
stay by Mi Young's side.

453
00:33:15,193 --> 00:33:17,995
I know.

454
00:33:17,996 --> 00:33:19,563
That's why I'm here.

455
00:33:19,698 --> 00:33:21,732
I need to discuss something with you.

456
00:33:22,267 --> 00:33:24,501
(Jihwaja Motel)

457
00:33:27,439 --> 00:33:30,107
Today, I'm not talking to you
as your brother,

458
00:33:30,409 --> 00:33:32,042
but as someone with more experience.

459
00:33:34,379 --> 00:33:35,679
Give everything up.

460
00:33:36,448 --> 00:33:38,616
That's the only way you can
get back together with her.

461
00:33:38,985 --> 00:33:41,819
I've already given up everything.

462
00:33:41,989 --> 00:33:45,790
You have to show her
that you'll do anything for her.

463
00:33:46,725 --> 00:33:48,659
Even things you would never do.

464
00:33:49,062 --> 00:33:51,162
Things I would never do?

465
00:33:51,631 --> 00:33:53,931
My wife once told me something.

466
00:33:54,700 --> 00:33:57,468
When I blew through all my money
trying to make a movie,

467
00:33:58,270 --> 00:34:01,505
she told me to take
a manual labor job if I had to,

468
00:34:02,140 --> 00:34:03,941
at least to earn enough
for Ha Neul's formula.

469
00:34:05,211 --> 00:34:06,078
But I told her...

470
00:34:06,878 --> 00:34:08,378
I couldn't bring myself to do it.

471
00:34:08,948 --> 00:34:10,648
Right. I remember that.

472
00:34:11,950 --> 00:34:13,584
Your wife went through a lot.

473
00:34:14,354 --> 00:34:16,353
But looking back,
I think that's when it happened.

474
00:34:16,988 --> 00:34:19,122
That's when my wife
completely gave up on me.

475
00:34:20,493 --> 00:34:21,727
She just wanted to see...

476
00:34:21,960 --> 00:34:24,361
my willingness to step up as a provider.

477
00:34:25,130 --> 00:34:26,664
When I refused,

478
00:34:27,599 --> 00:34:31,068
I think she realized
there was no hope for me.

479
00:34:34,372 --> 00:34:35,806
I'm such a piece of trash.

480
00:34:37,843 --> 00:34:41,178
Come to think of it,
all I've ever done is disappoint Mi Young.

481
00:34:54,693 --> 00:34:56,661
Why are you suddenly appearing
on a variety show?

482
00:34:56,862 --> 00:34:58,362
That fell through, didn't it?

483
00:34:58,597 --> 00:35:00,397
Fell through?

484
00:35:00,398 --> 00:35:02,733
I called the producer again,
worked everything out,

485
00:35:02,734 --> 00:35:05,036
and even got
the entire recording schedule set.

486
00:35:05,270 --> 00:35:06,129
Already?

487
00:35:06,379 --> 00:35:08,383
You even set the recording schedule?

488
00:35:08,408 --> 00:35:10,008
Of course. Who do you think I am?

489
00:35:10,038 --> 00:35:11,081
It's me, after all.

490
00:35:12,878 --> 00:35:14,846
Why the sudden change?

491
00:35:15,946 --> 00:35:18,548
You said you'd rather die
than make a fool of yourself on air.

492
00:35:18,817 --> 00:35:21,285
I barely convinced you last time,
only for it to fall through.

493
00:35:21,553 --> 00:35:22,753
Why are you doing it now?

494
00:35:25,924 --> 00:35:27,458
There's nothing I won't do anymore.

495
00:35:29,227 --> 00:35:31,762
From now on, I'll do whatever it takes.

496
00:35:32,030 --> 00:35:33,797
For J&WHITE, and...

497
00:35:35,033 --> 00:35:36,367
for you, Mi Young.

498
00:35:38,637 --> 00:35:40,838
Anyway, let's prepare well for the show...

499
00:35:40,839 --> 00:35:42,941
and really make this
a huge success for the brand.

500
00:35:42,942 --> 00:35:43,807
Let's go.

501
00:35:47,512 --> 00:35:49,380
Hello, is this the event company?

502
00:35:49,881 --> 00:35:52,216
I'm calling to inquire about something.

503
00:35:52,618 --> 00:35:54,318
I'm thinking of holding an event.

504
00:35:55,086 --> 00:35:58,022
I'm sorry. I'll call you
back in a little while.

505
00:35:59,624 --> 00:36:02,726
Are you going to keep pretending
you don't know me?

506
00:36:02,962 --> 00:36:04,362
When did I pretend not to know you?

507
00:36:04,897 --> 00:36:08,165
Is Won Ho really trying to get
back together with Mi Young?

508
00:36:09,067 --> 00:36:11,468
What? How did you know?

509
00:36:12,269 --> 00:36:13,604
Please, I'm begging you...

510
00:36:13,605 --> 00:36:16,240
Would I ever stand
in the way of my own child?

511
00:36:16,374 --> 00:36:18,542
I'd be happy if they worked things out.

512
00:36:19,244 --> 00:36:21,044
- Really?
- Do you think I'm lying?

513
00:36:21,946 --> 00:36:24,214
So what are you planning to do?

514
00:36:24,449 --> 00:36:25,649
Tell me everything.

515
00:36:27,185 --> 00:36:28,585
Go ahead.

516
00:36:29,054 --> 00:36:31,022
Well.

517
00:36:31,423 --> 00:36:33,858
Won Ho wants to...

518
00:36:35,026 --> 00:36:36,860
I desperately need your help.

519
00:36:37,195 --> 00:36:38,162
Okay?

520
00:36:38,163 --> 00:36:40,998
I need you two to back me up,

521
00:36:40,999 --> 00:36:43,501
so the event goes well that day.

522
00:36:44,903 --> 00:36:46,404
My goodness.

523
00:36:46,405 --> 00:36:50,040
And please keep this a secret
from Mrs. Baek.

524
00:36:50,041 --> 00:36:51,642
Don't worry, Mr. Ji.

525
00:36:51,776 --> 00:36:53,176
I'll keep it a secret.

526
00:36:54,946 --> 00:36:56,747
Why am I the one getting excited?

527
00:37:00,885 --> 00:37:03,420
But what's with that look
on your face, Mr. Kang?

528
00:37:04,222 --> 00:37:05,756
Are you sick?

529
00:37:05,757 --> 00:37:07,391
No, I'm not.

530
00:37:07,859 --> 00:37:09,859
I'm just nervous
about whether I can pull this off.

531
00:37:10,496 --> 00:37:13,297
Why are you nervous?
I should be the one who's nervous.

532
00:37:23,208 --> 00:37:24,141
Mrs. Baek.

533
00:37:24,710 --> 00:37:25,543
Yes.

534
00:37:29,080 --> 00:37:30,147
A delivery's here.

535
00:37:30,448 --> 00:37:32,449
Please put it here.

536
00:37:45,663 --> 00:37:48,265
(Nourishing Tonic, Korean Medicine Clinic)

537
00:38:02,747 --> 00:38:04,081
(Nourishing Tonic)

538
00:38:04,082 --> 00:38:06,717
I'm a little hesitant
to take that medicine.

539
00:38:07,219 --> 00:38:10,687
Every time I take it, I feel nauseous...

540
00:38:10,955 --> 00:38:12,188
and sick to my stomach.

541
00:38:27,806 --> 00:38:31,275
Please save my baby!

542
00:38:31,910 --> 00:38:34,011
My baby is going to be okay, right?

543
00:38:34,012 --> 00:38:37,347
Please save my baby!

544
00:38:38,650 --> 00:38:39,717
Have you...

545
00:38:40,752 --> 00:38:44,021
taken any medication recently?

546
00:38:44,856 --> 00:38:46,490
Medication?

547
00:38:53,198 --> 00:38:54,765
(Mi Sun)

548
00:39:02,006 --> 00:39:03,139
Hello.

549
00:39:03,308 --> 00:39:05,709
So, did you get the herbal medicine?

550
00:39:06,411 --> 00:39:09,446
Yes, I did. But...

551
00:39:10,950 --> 00:39:12,416
why did you send it?

552
00:39:12,417 --> 00:39:15,652
Why did I send it? To cheer you on.

553
00:39:16,888 --> 00:39:18,021
Cheer me on?

554
00:39:18,223 --> 00:39:20,691
You're spending time
with Won Ho these days, right?

555
00:39:21,460 --> 00:39:23,461
There's no need to be embarrassed.

556
00:39:23,462 --> 00:39:25,096
That's what married couples do.

557
00:39:25,831 --> 00:39:28,866
They say married couples
always make up after a fight.

558
00:39:29,267 --> 00:39:32,069
Why don't you just have
a baby while you're at it?

559
00:39:32,437 --> 00:39:34,638
Then you won't be talking
about breaking up again.

560
00:39:35,774 --> 00:39:36,741
Well.

561
00:39:37,108 --> 00:39:39,810
You know how much Won Ho loves children.

562
00:39:40,111 --> 00:39:41,945
There's no need to say more.

563
00:39:42,181 --> 00:39:44,849
If you take that regularly,
you'll have a baby in no time.

564
00:39:45,249 --> 00:39:48,251
Anyway, you're probably busy,
so I'll let you go.

565
00:40:03,802 --> 00:40:04,768
What's this?

566
00:40:05,336 --> 00:40:06,737
I'm not into this kind of thing.

567
00:40:07,338 --> 00:40:10,473
That's not a gift. It's evidence.

568
00:40:10,875 --> 00:40:12,576
Evidence...

569
00:40:13,044 --> 00:40:15,312
that a man named Kang Kyung Tae
pushed me off a cliff.

570
00:40:16,315 --> 00:40:17,314
Kang Kyung Tae?

571
00:40:17,550 --> 00:40:20,017
The man in the footage you gave me.

572
00:40:20,719 --> 00:40:22,920
His name is Kang Kyung Tae.

573
00:40:23,989 --> 00:40:25,388
He's also...

574
00:40:26,358 --> 00:40:27,824
one of Won Ho's closest friends.

575
00:40:28,894 --> 00:40:29,793
And?

576
00:40:30,328 --> 00:40:31,228
Get him for me.

577
00:40:32,296 --> 00:40:33,697
Kang Kyung Tae.

578
00:40:33,899 --> 00:40:36,533
- Me?
- Then I'll help you in return.

579
00:40:37,503 --> 00:40:39,437
So you and Mi Young...

580
00:40:40,038 --> 00:40:41,238
can get back together.

581
00:40:41,906 --> 00:40:42,740
What?

582
00:40:43,708 --> 00:40:44,708
Don't you know?

583
00:40:45,210 --> 00:40:47,011
Mr. Ji and Ms. Baek...

584
00:40:47,478 --> 00:40:48,779
are back together.

585
00:40:49,137 --> 00:40:51,134
He won't even take my calls these days.

586
00:40:52,116 --> 00:40:53,116
Still,

587
00:40:53,685 --> 00:40:55,419
breaking the two of them apart?

588
00:40:56,321 --> 00:40:58,088
I could do that in a heartbeat.

589
00:40:59,391 --> 00:41:01,125
I've already done it a few times.

590
00:41:02,293 --> 00:41:03,193
Help me.

591
00:41:04,162 --> 00:41:05,428
Then I'll...

592
00:41:06,797 --> 00:41:07,897
help you too.

593
00:41:08,167 --> 00:41:10,801
Is this your idea of asking someone
to save your life?

594
00:41:11,102 --> 00:41:12,536
Are you in or out?

595
00:41:13,872 --> 00:41:14,839
I'll think about it.

596
00:41:18,769 --> 00:41:20,403
If I stop answering my phone,

597
00:41:21,432 --> 00:41:23,600
just assume that man got to me.

598
00:41:33,191 --> 00:41:34,057
Don't you know?

599
00:41:34,859 --> 00:41:38,495
Mr. Ji and Ms. Baek are back together.

600
00:41:56,114 --> 00:41:58,148
(CEO Baek Mi Young)

601
00:42:02,571 --> 00:42:03,403
(Calvin)

602
00:42:03,487 --> 00:42:04,688
Are you free tonight?

603
00:42:05,790 --> 00:42:07,258
There's something I need to tell you.

604
00:42:14,999 --> 00:42:15,833
Do you remember?

605
00:42:18,202 --> 00:42:20,837
The day we came back from studying abroad.

606
00:42:23,708 --> 00:42:25,309
We stood right here,

607
00:42:26,111 --> 00:42:28,812
looking down over Seoul just like this.

608
00:42:29,847 --> 00:42:30,847
You said in ten years,

609
00:42:31,282 --> 00:42:34,384
you'd be the most famous female tailor
in Korea,

610
00:42:34,886 --> 00:42:35,719
and I...

611
00:42:36,521 --> 00:42:39,322
would own the best hotel in the country.

612
00:42:40,124 --> 00:42:42,393
Back then, we believed...

613
00:42:44,229 --> 00:42:46,296
we could do and be anything we wanted.

614
00:42:47,431 --> 00:42:51,368
I had no idea back then
that getting what you want...

615
00:42:52,570 --> 00:42:53,703
could be this hard.

616
00:42:54,839 --> 00:42:56,039
It's not too late.

617
00:42:57,614 --> 00:42:58,681
And you still...

618
00:42:59,678 --> 00:43:00,777
have a chance.

619
00:43:01,958 --> 00:43:04,393
Me. Calvin is your second chance.

620
00:43:07,151 --> 00:43:08,118
Calvin...

621
00:43:09,939 --> 00:43:12,139
I'm sorry, but like I told you
last time...

622
00:43:12,164 --> 00:43:13,458
I intend to keep my promise.

623
00:43:20,064 --> 00:43:21,097
This ring...

624
00:43:21,933 --> 00:43:23,400
Your mother gave it to me.

625
00:43:30,441 --> 00:43:32,208
She slipped it on my finger...

626
00:43:33,143 --> 00:43:35,278
and made me promise
to look after you to the end.

627
00:43:37,087 --> 00:43:38,483
I'm not taking it off.

628
00:43:41,953 --> 00:43:43,153
I've thought this through,

629
00:43:44,255 --> 00:43:45,789
and I know it's the right choice.

630
00:43:46,624 --> 00:43:48,792
For you, for me,

631
00:43:50,295 --> 00:43:51,628
and for your parents...

632
00:43:52,430 --> 00:43:53,764
watching over us from above.

633
00:43:54,833 --> 00:43:55,799
Calvin...

634
00:43:58,536 --> 00:43:59,736
Lean on me, Mi Young.

635
00:44:01,573 --> 00:44:03,172
I won't let you down.

636
00:44:04,909 --> 00:44:06,010
For the rest of my life,

637
00:44:06,844 --> 00:44:08,212
my only dream...

638
00:44:10,048 --> 00:44:10,881
is you.

639
00:44:23,228 --> 00:44:27,097
Being part of this "Dream Project"
truly felt like a dream.

640
00:44:27,098 --> 00:44:31,835
And seeing our bride and groom
turn it into such a beautiful reality...

641
00:44:32,053 --> 00:44:34,087
made me so genuinely happy.
Thank you both.

642
00:44:34,171 --> 00:44:35,071
Thank you.

643
00:44:36,240 --> 00:44:37,173
Thank you so much.

644
00:44:37,174 --> 00:44:39,542
Great work, everyone!

645
00:44:39,543 --> 00:44:41,978
You two worked so hard today.

646
00:44:41,979 --> 00:44:44,013
The footage turned out incredible.

647
00:44:44,014 --> 00:44:45,949
This is going to be a massive hit!

648
00:44:46,584 --> 00:44:49,786
It's all because Ms. Baek prepared
everything so meticulously.

649
00:44:50,888 --> 00:44:51,755
Did she now?

650
00:44:51,756 --> 00:44:55,058
My goodness, Mr. Ji, always so thoughtful!

651
00:44:56,461 --> 00:44:58,595
All right then, everyone.
Fantastic job today,

652
00:44:58,596 --> 00:44:59,596
and that is officially a wrap...

653
00:45:01,916 --> 00:45:03,684
Wait, actually,

654
00:45:03,768 --> 00:45:05,101
we have one last thing.

655
00:45:06,370 --> 00:45:07,437
One more?

656
00:45:07,539 --> 00:45:09,539
That's right, a bonus scene.

657
00:45:10,007 --> 00:45:12,208
This one is a solo take for Mr. Ji.

658
00:45:12,510 --> 00:45:13,843
Right this way, Mr. Ji.

659
00:45:18,850 --> 00:45:19,983
A bonus clip?

660
00:45:20,585 --> 00:45:21,818
You didn't mention this to me.

661
00:45:22,019 --> 00:45:23,987
Oh, didn't I?

662
00:45:25,957 --> 00:45:27,391
Auntie!

663
00:45:28,226 --> 00:45:30,460
Ha Neul. What are you doing here?

664
00:45:30,461 --> 00:45:32,362
I missed you so much.

665
00:45:34,303 --> 00:45:38,239
Seung Ho, Mi Sun,
what brings you two here?

666
00:45:38,415 --> 00:45:39,315
Beats me.

667
00:45:39,758 --> 00:45:41,491
I have no idea why I'm here either.

668
00:45:47,845 --> 00:45:50,046
Why is Won Ho up there?

669
00:45:50,215 --> 00:45:52,716
Won Ho never sings, you know that.

670
00:45:52,717 --> 00:45:54,384
This is a first for me too.

671
00:45:56,971 --> 00:46:01,241
<i>Through your tears, you told me</i>

672
00:46:01,325 --> 00:46:05,528
<i>You were leaving because you loved me</i>

673
00:46:06,497 --> 00:46:09,599
<i>I couldn't believe my ears</i>

674
00:46:11,636 --> 00:46:15,272
<i>Yet seeing you, my whole world</i>

675
00:46:15,273 --> 00:46:19,643
<i>In so much pain</i>

676
00:46:20,344 --> 00:46:23,646
<i>I couldn't bring myself to hold you back</i>

677
00:46:24,782 --> 00:46:28,785
<i>If it was truly meant for me</i>

678
00:46:28,869 --> 00:46:31,771
<i>Whose life holds nothing but you</i>

679
00:46:32,323 --> 00:46:34,524
Get off me.
Stop hiding behind the business!

680
00:46:34,525 --> 00:46:36,760
Every bit of this happened
because of your own greed!

681
00:46:36,761 --> 00:46:38,862
I said, let's get a divorce!

682
00:46:40,598 --> 00:46:42,132
Have you lost your mind?

683
00:46:42,133 --> 00:46:43,567
Are you actually going
to the Calvin Hotel right now?

684
00:46:43,568 --> 00:46:46,870
I said I'm going to the Calvin Hotel.
Did I say I was going with him?

685
00:46:46,871 --> 00:46:48,405
Then go ahead. See what happens!

686
00:46:48,406 --> 00:46:50,774
- How dare you!
- That's assault!

687
00:46:50,775 --> 00:46:53,176
You really get a kick out of calling me
a murderer, don't you?

688
00:46:53,411 --> 00:46:55,212
No, you'll have to hear it.

689
00:46:55,513 --> 00:46:57,280
Because I'm going to tear apart...

690
00:46:57,281 --> 00:46:58,882
that pathetic delusion of yours.

691
00:46:58,883 --> 00:47:00,417
Apologize to Dal Rae!

692
00:47:00,652 --> 00:47:01,718
And then what?

693
00:47:02,270 --> 00:47:03,804
Does that bring Dal Rae back
from the dead?

694
00:47:03,888 --> 00:47:07,457
<i>If only I have you</i>

695
00:47:09,093 --> 00:47:12,695
<i>The times we spent laughing together</i>

696
00:47:13,097 --> 00:47:14,064
Let go!

697
00:47:14,398 --> 00:47:15,332
Let go of me!

698
00:47:15,333 --> 00:47:16,467
Get a grip!

699
00:47:17,835 --> 00:47:23,006
<i>I will remember them forever</i>

700
00:47:23,007 --> 00:47:26,509
<i>Please think about it one more time</i>

701
00:47:26,510 --> 00:47:31,347
<i>Deep down, you already know</i>

702
00:47:31,716 --> 00:47:34,418
<i>What is truly best for me</i>

703
00:47:36,921 --> 00:47:43,426
<i>Please stay by my side</i>

704
00:47:44,762 --> 00:47:50,166
<i>Please don't walk away</i>

705
00:47:50,475 --> 00:47:54,304
<i>Even if I lose everything</i>

706
00:47:54,305 --> 00:47:57,707
<i>In this world, it doesn't matter</i>

707
00:47:57,708 --> 00:48:01,177
<i>As long as I have you</i>

708
00:48:01,261 --> 00:48:05,264
<i>As long as I have you</i>

709
00:48:13,124 --> 00:48:15,726
It feels like the first time
I've said this to you in seven years.

710
00:48:19,263 --> 00:48:20,397
My heart is pounding.

711
00:48:28,172 --> 00:48:29,105
Mi Young.

712
00:48:30,374 --> 00:48:32,875
I want to spend the rest of my life
by your side.

713
00:48:34,845 --> 00:48:36,546
If you feel the same way,

714
00:48:38,716 --> 00:48:41,151
will you please take my hand?

715
00:48:50,127 --> 00:48:51,227
I'll do it.

716
00:48:55,466 --> 00:48:56,733
Thank you, Mi Young.

717
00:49:05,543 --> 00:49:06,811
I'll give you a divorce.

718
00:49:07,945 --> 00:49:08,811
What?

719
00:49:11,182 --> 00:49:12,149
I'm...

720
00:49:14,418 --> 00:49:15,818
going to divorce you.

721
00:49:16,091 --> 00:49:17,421
- Goodness...
- What?

722
00:49:19,958 --> 00:49:21,157
What's going on?

723
00:49:22,638 --> 00:49:23,461
Wait...

724
00:49:25,056 --> 00:49:26,230
This isn't right.

725
00:49:27,865 --> 00:49:28,731
Hold on.

726
00:49:29,800 --> 00:49:31,534
Mi Young, talk to me.

727
00:49:31,769 --> 00:49:33,204
I have nothing left to say to you.

728
00:49:33,537 --> 00:49:34,839
Mi Young, please!

729
00:49:37,007 --> 00:49:37,907
Fine, I get it.

730
00:49:37,908 --> 00:49:41,811
I know I'm still nowhere near
good enough for you,

731
00:49:41,812 --> 00:49:42,745
but...

732
00:49:43,747 --> 00:49:45,882
is there really no way back for us?

733
00:49:46,884 --> 00:49:49,919
No. There isn't.

734
00:49:50,555 --> 00:49:52,989
Then why would you...

735
00:49:53,758 --> 00:49:56,159
Things were good between us.
We were doing so well.

736
00:49:56,761 --> 00:49:58,462
I'm sorry if I hurt you.

737
00:49:58,766 --> 00:50:00,863
What is it then?
Tell me what the problem is.

738
00:50:00,864 --> 00:50:02,632
Just tell me. I'll take care of it.

739
00:50:02,633 --> 00:50:03,533
I'll make it right.

740
00:50:06,570 --> 00:50:08,337
I just can't read you, Mi Young.

741
00:50:08,523 --> 00:50:10,616
When will I ever truly understand
how you feel?

742
00:50:10,641 --> 00:50:13,342
Am I really supposed
to let you go like this?

743
00:50:13,778 --> 00:50:14,678
I...

744
00:50:15,746 --> 00:50:17,448
I want to stay with you too.

745
00:50:17,449 --> 00:50:20,250
Then why ask for a divorce? Why?

746
00:50:20,251 --> 00:50:21,685
I can't have children!

747
00:50:24,222 --> 00:50:25,811
No matter what I do,

748
00:50:25,835 --> 00:50:27,757
I can never carry your child again,
Won Ho!

749
00:50:29,326 --> 00:50:30,226
What?

750
00:50:30,561 --> 00:50:31,962
Ever since we lost Dal Rae,

751
00:50:33,063 --> 00:50:35,531
I can't have any more children.

752
00:50:39,036 --> 00:50:40,738
I only found out later.

753
00:50:42,373 --> 00:50:43,239
I...

754
00:50:44,576 --> 00:50:47,410
I can't put you through that, Won Ho.

755
00:50:49,180 --> 00:50:50,781
I don't care about starting over!

756
00:50:51,282 --> 00:50:52,948
What are you talking about?

757
00:50:52,949 --> 00:50:55,217
When did I ever pressure you into that?

758
00:50:55,619 --> 00:50:57,720
I only need you.

759
00:50:58,389 --> 00:50:59,957
My mind is made up.

760
00:51:00,524 --> 00:51:01,457
I'm sorry.

761
00:51:01,693 --> 00:51:03,426
Mi Young, please don't do this. Don't go.

762
00:51:03,729 --> 00:51:06,329
What am I supposed to do
if you walk away like this?

763
00:51:06,564 --> 00:51:07,998
What am I supposed to do?

764
00:51:08,632 --> 00:51:09,565
I...

765
00:51:11,202 --> 00:51:13,270
I want to make you happy, Won Ho.

766
00:51:13,938 --> 00:51:15,572
I want to see you smile again.

767
00:51:15,573 --> 00:51:18,408
I want us to live like everyone else.

768
00:51:18,409 --> 00:51:21,378
But the way I am now,
I can't do that for you.

769
00:51:21,379 --> 00:51:22,279
I...

770
00:51:23,447 --> 00:51:24,414
I just can't.

771
00:51:25,182 --> 00:51:27,450
You don't have to do
a single thing for me!

772
00:51:27,952 --> 00:51:30,520
Just stay by my side! That's all I need!

773
00:51:31,455 --> 00:51:32,455
Please...

774
00:51:33,991 --> 00:51:35,291
Please let me go.

775
00:51:36,026 --> 00:51:38,627
Don't go. I said don't go!

776
00:51:38,628 --> 00:51:39,897
Don't walk away!

777
00:52:06,724 --> 00:52:07,724
We're here.

778
00:52:08,932 --> 00:52:10,132
Are you all right?

779
00:52:10,761 --> 00:52:12,233
How much did you drink tonight?

780
00:52:12,258 --> 00:52:13,230
Good grief!

781
00:52:14,465 --> 00:52:15,765
How much did he have?

782
00:52:15,766 --> 00:52:17,600
- Are you all right?
- Pull yourself together!

783
00:52:17,601 --> 00:52:18,768
- Get the door.
- Okay.

784
00:52:19,103 --> 00:52:20,303
Won Ho, wake up!

785
00:52:21,205 --> 00:52:22,172
Seriously...

786
00:52:26,844 --> 00:52:28,812
Why'd you drink yourself
into this state, you idiot?

787
00:52:28,813 --> 00:52:29,913
Where am I?

788
00:52:30,481 --> 00:52:31,849
Kyung Tae, let's have one more round.

789
00:52:31,850 --> 00:52:32,749
No, Won Ho.

790
00:52:33,117 --> 00:52:35,351
- You need to sleep this off.
- I don't need sleep.

791
00:52:35,352 --> 00:52:37,188
Hey, stay still.

792
00:52:37,189 --> 00:52:38,521
Just go to sleep.

793
00:52:38,522 --> 00:52:40,990
I can't sleep! Not tonight!

794
00:52:40,991 --> 00:52:42,526
What is all this racket?

795
00:52:44,895 --> 00:52:46,596
What, you got dumped
by a woman like Mi Young,

796
00:52:46,597 --> 00:52:48,431
and now you're drinking
yourself senseless?

797
00:52:48,432 --> 00:52:50,067
Don't talk about Mi Young like that!

798
00:52:52,002 --> 00:52:54,070
What did Mi Young ever do to you?

799
00:52:54,571 --> 00:52:56,339
Was marrying me...

800
00:52:57,308 --> 00:52:59,142
really such a mistake on her part?

801
00:52:59,143 --> 00:53:00,143
Yes, it was!

802
00:53:00,545 --> 00:53:02,211
You married your precious Mi Young,

803
00:53:02,212 --> 00:53:04,114
and look at you now. What a triumph!

804
00:53:07,418 --> 00:53:08,819
And honestly, Mi Young is no better.

805
00:53:09,187 --> 00:53:11,287
I even sent her herbal medicine
so she could conceive.

806
00:53:11,923 --> 00:53:14,124
She never thinks of anyone
but herself, I swear.

807
00:53:14,491 --> 00:53:15,424
What?

808
00:53:16,493 --> 00:53:18,027
You sent what to Mi Young?

809
00:53:20,230 --> 00:53:22,098
Won Ho, you're wasted.

810
00:53:22,099 --> 00:53:23,333
You need to go to bed now.

811
00:53:23,568 --> 00:53:24,834
Get off me!

812
00:53:24,835 --> 00:53:27,904
Mi Young left me because of you, Mother!

813
00:53:27,905 --> 00:53:29,873
What did you just say? Because of me?

814
00:53:31,609 --> 00:53:33,543
Ms. Ryu, I'll take my leave now.

815
00:53:37,281 --> 00:53:38,448
Say that again.

816
00:53:39,082 --> 00:53:41,183
What on earth did I ever do to Mi Young?

817
00:53:41,485 --> 00:53:42,452
Looked down on her.

818
00:53:43,420 --> 00:53:44,487
You treated her like dirt.

819
00:53:44,922 --> 00:53:45,855
Excuse me?

820
00:53:46,490 --> 00:53:49,325
Mi Young wanted this marriage to work,

821
00:53:50,929 --> 00:53:53,263
so she bent over backward
to please you, Mother.

822
00:53:55,099 --> 00:53:57,534
Even though you hated her guts,

823
00:53:59,203 --> 00:54:02,772
she gave you everything she had.

824
00:54:03,741 --> 00:54:05,842
And what did you do in return?

825
00:54:06,778 --> 00:54:08,645
When she was broken and falling apart,

826
00:54:09,647 --> 00:54:11,414
you completely turned your back on her.

827
00:54:11,415 --> 00:54:12,982
When did I ever turn my back on her?

828
00:54:12,983 --> 00:54:14,884
After what happened to Dal Rae!

829
00:54:16,020 --> 00:54:18,421
After Dal Rae died
and Mi Young was drowning in grief,

830
00:54:20,758 --> 00:54:22,358
what did you ever do for her?

831
00:54:23,794 --> 00:54:25,562
When she couldn't swallow
a single bite of food,

832
00:54:26,563 --> 00:54:28,365
did you ever bring her a bowl of soup?

833
00:54:31,101 --> 00:54:32,368
Did you ever...

834
00:54:33,169 --> 00:54:35,404
even once tell her it would be okay?

835
00:54:37,341 --> 00:54:39,975
Did you ever hold her in your arms?

836
00:54:41,445 --> 00:54:44,947
You never checked on her. Not once!

837
00:54:48,485 --> 00:54:50,053
And now you stand here saying what?

838
00:54:50,955 --> 00:54:52,823
You sent her fertility medicine?

839
00:54:53,824 --> 00:54:57,060
Mother... Mother!

840
00:54:58,096 --> 00:55:00,130
Do you think Mi Young is a joke?

841
00:55:00,898 --> 00:55:03,200
Listen to what's coming out
of your mouth right now!

842
00:55:03,635 --> 00:55:06,636
Even I wouldn't stay!

843
00:55:08,238 --> 00:55:10,072
If I were Mi Young,

844
00:55:10,674 --> 00:55:12,785
I wouldn't want to be your daughter-in-law
for another second!

845
00:55:12,810 --> 00:55:14,844
Never again!

846
00:56:01,658 --> 00:56:02,592
Damn it.

847
00:56:23,413 --> 00:56:24,680
I'll instruct...

848
00:56:25,949 --> 00:56:26,815
my lawyer...

849
00:56:28,218 --> 00:56:30,119
to proceed with the trial as planned.

850
00:56:31,121 --> 00:56:33,189
And I'm stepping down from the company.

851
00:56:33,957 --> 00:56:34,990
Must be nice.

852
00:56:35,792 --> 00:56:37,427
Having everything come so easily to you.

853
00:56:37,995 --> 00:56:40,264
I'll make sure the handover is
completely seamless,

854
00:56:42,633 --> 00:56:44,100
so don't worry.

855
00:57:08,692 --> 00:57:10,392
If I stop answering my phone,

856
00:57:11,262 --> 00:57:13,896
just assume that man got to me.

857
00:57:18,902 --> 00:57:20,202
(An Hee Ju)

858
00:57:29,947 --> 00:57:31,581
Mr. Ji...

859
00:57:32,749 --> 00:57:34,918
Yes, what's going on?

860
00:57:35,786 --> 00:57:38,855
The other day, Mi Young mentioned that...

861
00:57:39,623 --> 00:57:43,392
the herbal medicine you prepared for her
three years ago...

862
00:57:45,663 --> 00:57:49,298
it was actually Kyung Tae
who brought it over.

863
00:57:49,666 --> 00:57:52,067
Yes, that's right. Why bring that up now?

864
00:57:52,603 --> 00:57:54,470
Well, the thing is...

865
00:57:57,875 --> 00:58:00,610
Something has been bothering me,

866
00:58:01,945 --> 00:58:04,780
and I felt like I had to tell you.

867
00:58:15,158 --> 00:58:16,992
Won Ho. Did you want to see me?

868
00:58:18,228 --> 00:58:20,330
Is there something you're keeping from me?

869
00:58:21,933 --> 00:58:22,865
What?

870
00:58:25,903 --> 00:58:28,004
Care to explain what all this means?

871
00:58:34,711 --> 00:58:35,577
Won Ho...

872
00:58:36,013 --> 00:58:37,480
Do you have feelings for Mi Young?

873
00:58:38,115 --> 00:58:39,582
No, it's not like that.

874
00:58:40,684 --> 00:58:42,652
The medicine that caused her miscarriage.

875
00:58:44,288 --> 00:58:45,488
Did you do that too?

876
00:58:45,489 --> 00:58:47,023
No, I didn't.

877
00:58:47,658 --> 00:58:49,425
What are you talking about?
How could you accuse me of that?

878
00:58:49,426 --> 00:58:51,093
Then how do you explain this?

879
00:58:51,728 --> 00:58:53,930
Pulling this kind of crap behind my back!

880
00:58:54,531 --> 00:58:56,133
How am I supposed to trust a word you say?

881
00:58:56,733 --> 00:58:57,968
Do you honestly believe...

882
00:58:58,235 --> 00:59:02,071
I swapped out her medicine
just to cause a miscarriage?

883
00:59:03,207 --> 00:59:04,173
Is that it?

884
00:59:05,876 --> 00:59:06,909
What?

885
00:59:08,512 --> 00:59:09,412
The door's unlocked.

886
00:59:25,395 --> 00:59:26,495
Hee Ju!

887
00:59:27,331 --> 00:59:29,165
Are you okay? Hee Ju!

888
00:59:29,866 --> 00:59:31,435
That doesn't make any sense!

889
00:59:32,128 --> 00:59:35,063
If I really had feelings for Mi Young,
why would I do something so vile?

890
00:59:36,006 --> 00:59:37,940
Knowing full well
who would suffer the most?

891
00:59:39,209 --> 00:59:41,577
"Swapped out the medicine"?
What are you talking about?

892
00:59:42,713 --> 00:59:44,781
I never said anything
about swapping it out.

893
00:59:47,551 --> 00:59:48,484
Wait...

894
00:59:49,252 --> 00:59:50,252
It was you.

895
00:59:52,089 --> 00:59:53,490
Kyung Tae, it was you all along.

896
00:59:54,291 --> 00:59:56,325
You tampered with that medicine,

897
00:59:56,994 --> 00:59:58,962
and that's what made Mi Young
lose the baby.

898
01:00:01,999 --> 01:00:02,932
Won Ho...

899
01:00:05,102 --> 01:00:06,001
Why?

900
01:00:07,471 --> 01:00:08,905
Why on earth would you do that?

901
01:00:10,340 --> 01:00:11,307
Won Ho...

902
01:00:15,445 --> 01:00:16,780
Do you honestly...

903
01:00:18,783 --> 01:00:19,950
have no idea how I feel?

904
01:00:20,384 --> 01:00:21,651
Tell me, you bastard!

905
01:00:22,084 --> 01:00:24,653
Tell me why the hell
you did that to Mi Young!

906
01:00:29,693 --> 01:00:31,060
Just hang on a second.

907
01:00:31,628 --> 01:00:32,494
All right.

908
01:00:59,623 --> 01:01:01,258
The person I have feelings for...

909
01:01:03,126 --> 01:01:04,793
isn't your wife, Won Ho.

910
01:01:06,398 --> 01:01:07,364
Won Ho...

911
01:01:11,502 --> 01:01:12,635
Won Ho...

912
01:01:34,567 --> 01:01:37,569
(OK! Let's Get Divorced)

913
01:01:39,642 --> 01:01:42,010
Enough to throw away
what matters most to you?

914
01:01:42,365 --> 01:01:44,901
Seriously, Won Ho, is that really it?

915
01:01:44,902 --> 01:01:46,869
Selling off the company
without even talking to your wife?

916
01:01:46,893 --> 01:01:47,870
Have you lost your mind?

917
01:01:48,218 --> 01:01:51,153
To my husband and me, this company...

918
01:01:51,559 --> 01:01:52,558
is our baby.

919
01:01:52,642 --> 01:01:54,643
So Calvin, please help us.

920
01:01:56,346 --> 01:01:58,447
In return, that ring...

921
01:01:58,682 --> 01:02:01,717
I want it completely out of your life.

922
01:02:01,718 --> 01:02:03,552
Even if this is how our story ends,

923
01:02:03,787 --> 01:02:05,555
I still love you.

924
01:02:05,740 --> 01:02:07,490
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
